  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "new_object",
    "file": "libredwg/src/in_dxf.c",
    "description": "Root cause is ownership/lifetime misuse in DXF parsing: `new_object` stores pointers from transient `Dxf_Pair` string values (notably for common entity data used by POINTCLOUD, e.g. fields freed by `dwg_free_common_entity_data`) into the created DWG object, then unconditionally calls `dxf_free_pair(pair)` in the parse loop. This frees the same heap string once during parse, but the object still retains the dangling pointer and later `dwg_free_*` frees it again, causing double-free. Crash is observed in `dwg_free_common_entity_data` (`free.c:414` path), but the bug is in parser-side ownership handling in `new_object`.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires a DXF input (via `llvmfuzz` -> `dwg_read_dxf` -> `dxf_blocks_read` -> `new_object`) that creates a POINTCLOUD/entity object and assigns one or more string-backed fields from `pair->value.s` without duplicating/transferring ownership safely. After parsing, `new_object` frees each pair (`dxf_free_pair`), leaving dangling pointers in the object. When harness later calls `dwg_free`, object cleanup (`dwg_free_POINTCLOUD` -> `dwg_free_common_entity_data`) frees that stale pointer again, producing ASan double-free."
  },
